From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kk: name destroyed image views at render pass begin

STEAMAC-BJ/BK (1.9.14, Apple M5 Pro, DOOM (2016)): SIGSEGV at 0x48 in
transition_attachment+60 <- begin_subpass+2544 <-
vk_common_CmdBeginRenderPass2+2480 on the vkr ring thread. The faulting
instruction is `ldr w8, [x8, #0x48]` with x8 = image_view->image: the
attachment's view pointer was set, its image field NULL. libmalloc clears
freed blocks, so the framebuffer named an image view that had been
destroyed before the render pass began. A framebuffer whose view is
destroyed and then begun in a render pass faults at exactly these three
frames and offsets on the 1.9.14 driver. Who destroyed the view (the
game, or the guest's Venus driver) is not known.

Keep the set of live image views per device and check the attachments of
vkCmdBeginRenderPass2 against it before Mesa's common code dereferences
them. A view that is not alive is logged with its attachment index,
format, samples, source (framebuffer or imageless begin) and the
framebuffer. Recording is unchanged: this is diagnostic, not a fix of
the invalid use.

Regression: REPRO_CASE=sentry-bj REPRO_DRIVER=kosmickrisp
host/moltenvk/repro/run.sh <dylib>. A live view clears 16 pixels green
without a log line; a destroyed view is named before the fault. The
1.9.14 driver faults without naming it.

Generated-by: LLM
